nalistic-themed transmission by an unidentified station auto denominated çOddyntengis QMé. Unf\ortunately, the content could not be recorder, and the remaining info is only of family members and friends of the resident, which related two more occurrences before their disappearance. Because of that, it is speculated that the radio has the capability\ to contact up to infinite frequencies and/or use unknown elements as sources, creating bridges to the multiverse and transmitting it to its listeners.)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Arial 10 Tf)/DS(font: Arial,sans-serif 10.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240918165815-03'00')/NM(d7acb930cdb148c288da8a71ac95f1c3)/Page 1/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Arial;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:justify">It has all the functions of a common radio receiver, the way it was discovered by a resident of a house close to Flopper Lake was unusual, as it was catching frequencie\s of THF level \(on this instance, it was estimated to be around 24.960 GHz\) and unknown source. The resulting waves were curiously a hybrid of the radiation waves usually found in spectroscopy procedures and an \(according to the witnesses\) journalisti\c-themed transmission by an unidentified station auto denominated &#8220;Oddyntengis QM&#8221;. Unfortunately, the content could not be recorder, and the remaining info is only of family members and friends of the resident, which related two more occurren\ces before their disappearance. Because of that, it is speculated that the radio has the capability to contact up to infinite frequencies and/or use unknown elements as sources, creating bridges to the multiverse and transmitting it to its listeners.</spa\n></p></body>)/Rect[45.3301 100.864 571.312 206.874]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj46 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(   40)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 21.8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 21.8pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240909164321-03'00')/NM(1136aaeffc294a48afa27816b1ee9af3)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:21.8pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">   40</span></p></body>)/Rect[17.301 674.202 180.873 699.612]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj47 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(   Co)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 21.8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 21.8pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240909164335-03'00')/NM(e7a7212f000b47d5b3601cb1cf455d44)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:21.8pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">   Co</span></p></body>)/Rect[91.573 674.202 255.145 699.612]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj48 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(Transmission - The main function of a radio communicator. Can catch frequencies in a virtually infinite range, being able to cross dimensions if tuned to the right settings.)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 10 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 10.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240918165025-03'00')/NM(f830e9b47d1b4fc4ba9f423fdb15389f)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http:/